{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCHOOL SIGN-UP (story hero classroom card, classroom band)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
One email field that subscribes a teacher to a Klaviyo list (default: Schools Monthly Email Newsletter, XRcgpd) with
Klaviyo's client subscriptions API, the same call assets/back-in-stock.js uses. Handled in voxblock.js
(`[data-school-signup]`), which also sends PostHog `school_signup` { page, form }.

Params:
- form_id: short id, unique on the page (used for the input id and the `form` property)
- list_id: Klaviyo list id
- source: custom_source shown on the Klaviyo profile
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign list_id = list_id | default: 'XRcgpd'
  assign input_id = 'school-signup-' | append: form_id | append: '-' | append: section.id
-%}

<form class="school-signup" novalidate data-school-signup data-form="{{ form_id | escape }}" data-list-id="{{ list_id | escape }}" data-company-id="TKFEPz" data-source="{{ source | default: 'Story page' | escape }}">
  <div class="school-signup__row">
    <label for="{{ input_id }}" class="sr-only">{{ 'collection.school_signup.label' | t }}</label>
    <input id="{{ input_id }}" class="school-signup__input" type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" inputmode="email" required placeholder="{{ 'collection.school_signup.placeholder' | t }}">
    <button type="submit" class="series-button series-button--small school-signup__button">{{ 'collection.school_signup.button' | t }}</button>
  </div>
  <p class="school-signup__status" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden
    data-thanks="{{ 'collection.school_signup.thanks' | t | escape }}"
    data-error="{{ 'collection.school_signup.error' | t | escape }}"
    data-invalid="{{ 'collection.school_signup.invalid' | t | escape }}"></p>
</form>
